.TH PIN 1
.SH NAME
pin \- session-based terminal todo HUD for human-agent collaboration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pin
[--session SESSION] COMMAND [ARGS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Pin keeps a tiny append-only todo log in the current folder or git worktree. It is designed for humans working with Claude, Codex, tmux panes, and worktrees.
.PP
Core rule: agents report progress; humans pin task truth. Agent progress never marks work done.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add|a TITLE [-p PRIORITY] [-t TAG]
Add a task to the active session.
.TP
.B list|ls
List tasks in the active session.
.TP
.B show [ID]
Show the session HUD, or task details when ID is provided.
.TP
.B overlay|o
Open the terminal HUD. In tmux this uses display-popup.
.TP
.B sessions|ss
List active sessions in the current folder.
.TP
.B agent|ag ID AGENT STATUS BODY
Record agent progress without changing human task status.
.TP
.B report|ar ID -a AGENT BODY
Record an agent report and move the task to review.
.TP
.B brief|br
Print a pasteable handoff for Claude/Codex.
.TP
.B start|s ID, review|r ID, fail|f ID REASON, block|b ID REASON, verified|ok ID [NOTE], done|d|complete|completed ID, cancel|c ID
Human-owned status changes. Use done/complete for successfully closed work and cancel for work that no longer applies.
.SH SESSIONS
Use --session/-s or PIN_SESSION to scope work. Default session is "default".
.SH STORAGE
Per folder: .pin/meta.json and .pin/log.jsonl. Global registry: ~/.local/share/pin/registry.jsonl.
.SH LICENSE
MIT

.SH FILE REFERENCES
Search project files with:
.PP
.nf
pin files auth
pin find tokref
.fi
.PP
Use @ references in task text, notes, failures, and agent progress:
.PP
.nf
pin a "Fix redirect in @lgn" -t auth
pin n 1 "Repro is in @lgnsmk"
pin ag 1 claude working "Checking @tokref"
.fi
.PP
Attach or remove files explicitly:
.PP
.nf
pin ref 1 src/auth/login.rs
pin unref 1 src/auth/login.rs
.fi
